<h1>bozo sort</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A terribly inefficient <a href="sort.html"><em>sort</em></a> algorithm that randomly swaps items until they are in order.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="sort.html"><em>sort</em></a> algorithm, <a href="lasVegas.html"><em>Las Vegas algorithm</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="bogosort.html"><em>bogosort</em></a>, <a href="stoogesort.html"><em>stooge sort</em></a>, <a href="permutationSort.html"><em>permutation sort</em></a>, <a href="luckySort.html"><em>lucky sort</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Run time analysis in<br /> <strong>Hermann Gruber, Markus Holzer</strong>, and <strong>Oliver Ruepp</strong>, <em>Sorting the slow way: An analysis of perversely awful randomized sorting algorithms</em>, FUN 2007, LNCS 4475, pp. 183-197, 2007. <br /> Note: "Supercalifragilisticexpialidocious" is misspelled on the sixth page, although it is spelled correctly in the footnote.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Pat Morin's <a href="https://cglab.ca/~morin/misc/sortalg/" target="_blank">implementation (Java)</a>.

